207 - It May Be at Morn
 / 
Key: C
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 207
Topic: Jesus Christ - 

Verse 1:
[C]It may be at morn, when the day [G7]is awaking,
[C]When sunlight through darkness and shadow is breaking,
[C]That Jesus will come in the fullness of glory
[C]To receive from the world His own.

Refrain:
[C]O Lord Jesus, how long, how long
[C]Ere we shout the glad song?
[C/G]Christ returneth, [G]Hallelujah!
[G]Hallelujah! Amen, Hallelujah! Amen.

Verse 2:
[C]It may be at midday, it may [G7]be at twilight,
[C]It may be, perchance, that the blackness of midnight
[C]Will burst into light in the blaze of His glory,
[C]When Jesus receives His own.

Verse 3:
[C]O joy! O delight! should we [G7]go without dying,
[C]No sickness, no sadness, no dread, and no crying,
[C]Caught up through the clouds with our Lord into glory,
[C]When Jesus receives His own.
